Root cause:
The bug occurs in the error path of `gss_alloc_msg()` when `kstrdup_const()` fails. A previous commit added a `kref_get(&gss_auth->kref)` to balance the `gss_put_auth()` in `gss_release_msg()`, but no corresponding `kref_put()` was added in the `err_put_pipe_version` error label. This causes a kref leak, preventing the `gss_auth` structure from ever being freed.

Code statements information:
The code statements that lead to the bug are:
<text>kref_get(&gss_auth->kref);</text>
<text>err_put_pipe_version:</text>
<text>	put_pipe_version(gss_auth->net);</text>
<text>	kfree(gss_msg);</text>
Reason:
After kref_get() increments the reference count on gss_auth, if kstrdup_const() fails, the code jumps to the `err_put_pipe_version` label. That path calls `put_pipe_version()` and `kfree(gss_msg)` but lacks a corresponding `kref_put()`. This causes a kref leak, preventing the gss_auth structure from ever being freed.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
<text>+	kref_put(&gss_auth->kref, gss_free_callback);</text>
Reason:
Adding `kref_put(&gss_auth->kref, gss_free_callback)` in the `err_put_pipe_version` error path properly releases the reference that was obtained earlier by `kref_get()`, fixing the kref leak and allowing the gss_auth structure to be freed when its reference count reaches zero.


